  "notes": "If you live in the Williamson County part of Pflugerville, your elections office is Williamson County Elections, 301 SE Inner Loop, Georgetown, 512-943-1630. Pflugerville is in both Travis and Williamson counties, so check which county you're registered in before you pick a polling place. You must vote in your county of registration. Travis County: moved here from another Texas county and didn't re-register? You may be able to vote a limited ballot, but only at the Travis County Elections office, 5501 Airport Blvd., during early voting (through Oct 30); call 512-238-8683 first. Have a Travis mail ballot? On Election Day only, 7 AM to 7 PM, you can hand it in yourself, with photo ID, at 5501 Airport Blvd. Mail ballot questions: ebbm@traviscountytx.gov or 512-238-8683.",
